1
00:02:04,887 --> 00:02:08,947
No living creature was hurt during
the production of this show.

2
00:02:09,076 --> 00:02:16,536
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

3
00:02:16,887 --> 00:02:18,857
Osman!

4
00:02:20,199 --> 00:02:23,099
You have no place to escape!

5
00:02:28,869 --> 00:02:32,399
Son!
Son!

6
00:02:32,537 --> 00:02:35,637
Hold on.
Hold on.

7
00:02:43,294 --> 00:02:45,484
Archers!

8
00:02:47,672 --> 00:02:49,492
Archers!

9
00:02:50,898 --> 00:02:54,092
Alps!
Shields!

10
00:02:54,092 --> 00:02:56,132
Aim!

11
00:02:57,889 --> 00:02:59,509
Brother!

12
00:03:03,397 --> 00:03:05,547
Shoot!

13
00:03:06,119 --> 00:03:07,689
Defend!

14
00:03:08,293 --> 00:03:10,153
Aim!

15
00:03:13,238 --> 00:03:14,958
Shoot!

16
00:03:17,253 --> 00:03:20,473
Hold on! Hold on!

17
00:03:21,862 --> 00:03:23,772
Hold on!

18
00:03:27,885 --> 00:03:30,915
Flatyos!
Alps!

19
00:03:31,376 --> 00:03:33,256
Aim!

20
00:03:34,081 --> 00:03:35,701
Shoot!

21
00:03:43,768 --> 00:03:46,108
Hold on brothers!

22
00:03:48,018 --> 00:03:50,499
- Brother.
- Aim!

23
00:03:50,499 --> 00:03:53,269
- Brother.
- Shoot!

24
00:04:02,781 --> 00:04:04,631
Aim!

25
00:04:05,109 --> 00:04:06,899
Shoot!

26
00:04:20,838 --> 00:04:23,748
- Close up!
- Aim!

27
00:04:25,317 --> 00:04:27,037
Shoot!

28
00:04:30,470 --> 00:04:34,270
Hold on valiants!
Hold on son!

29
00:04:34,644 --> 00:04:37,094
Come on brothers, resist!

30
00:04:37,212 --> 00:04:41,146
My lion, hang on.

31
00:04:41,146 --> 00:04:43,216
Aim!

32
00:04:44,637 --> 00:04:47,117
Forward!

33
00:04:52,020 --> 00:04:56,510
- We must get out of here, brother!
- We will, brother, we will!

34
00:04:56,658 --> 00:05:00,678
- We have to leave here.
- Alps! Hang on!

35
00:05:03,362 --> 00:05:04,772
Hold on.

36
00:05:12,289 --> 00:05:14,469
Hold on my valiants!

37
00:05:19,775 --> 00:05:21,745
Move!

38
00:05:23,098 --> 00:05:25,138
Shields!

39
00:05:26,003 --> 00:05:28,543
Now!

40
00:05:30,134 --> 00:05:32,584
Now! Now!

41
00:05:32,648 --> 00:05:35,408
Now! Close up!

42
00:05:40,003 --> 00:05:42,273
Close up!

43
00:05:45,733 --> 00:05:49,313
Hold on brothers.
We will get out of here!

44
00:05:53,251 --> 00:05:55,061
Come on!

45
00:05:55,267 --> 00:05:58,767
Protect the woundeds!

46
00:05:58,867 --> 00:06:01,047
Come on Alps!

47
00:06:19,889 --> 00:06:23,259
Boran!
Protect me!

48
00:06:36,337 --> 00:06:38,147
Hold on.

49
00:06:41,026 --> 00:06:43,806
Pull the woundeds!

50
00:07:01,644 --> 00:07:03,424
Come on!

51
00:07:27,004 --> 00:07:29,541
- We are going to carry the woundeds!
- Come on son!

52
00:07:29,541 --> 00:07:31,801
Hold on everyone!

53
00:07:34,420 --> 00:07:38,090
- Hold on Bayhoca!
- He can't get up.

54
00:07:40,290 --> 00:07:42,770
Pull the woundeds!

55
00:07:46,079 --> 00:07:49,609
Pull!
Pull!

56
00:08:00,381 --> 00:08:02,671
- Baysungur!
- My Bey!

57
00:08:03,023 --> 00:08:06,053
Come on!
Pull!

58
00:08:11,343 --> 00:08:14,343
Everyone, move!

59
00:08:20,069 --> 00:08:21,919
Come on!

60
00:08:34,646 --> 00:08:38,046
- Help, Alps!
- Come on son!

61
00:08:40,997 --> 00:08:42,547
Close up!

62
00:08:49,111 --> 00:08:53,641
Ya Allah! Bismillahirrahmanirrahim
"In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful."

63
00:08:59,557 --> 00:09:01,777
Hold on Alps!

64
00:09:07,362 --> 00:09:09,192
Wait.

65
00:09:11,752 --> 00:09:13,802
Wait.

66
00:09:17,529 --> 00:09:19,849
Wait.

67
00:09:29,276 --> 00:09:31,546
Where were you?

68
00:09:40,790 --> 00:09:43,578
Where were you uncle?

69
00:09:43,578 --> 00:09:47,888
- I went to Nicola, nephew.
- What did you say?

70
00:09:50,202 --> 00:09:54,692
I said "Do you think I am a betrayer?" to
him so that he doesn't suspect me.

71
00:09:55,268 --> 00:09:59,488
It seems you are in the wrong way
to me, uncle.

72
00:10:01,119 --> 00:10:03,349
Osman must die.

73
00:10:04,500 --> 00:10:08,550
Osman must die.

74
00:10:09,861 --> 00:10:17,411
That Osman who take us to one war to
another, who set us against our own people

75
00:10:19,514 --> 00:10:21,754
He must die.

76
00:10:22,867 --> 00:10:26,487
You are worried about Aygül.

77
00:10:27,918 --> 00:10:29,768
You are right.

78
00:10:31,035 --> 00:10:37,275
However, she is going after her own
destiny.

79
00:10:39,952 --> 00:10:43,292
Do not tire yourself up.

80
00:10:43,489 --> 00:10:46,349
Do you think that is easy, Hatun?

81
00:10:47,179 --> 00:10:52,099
She is my beloved daughter.

82
00:10:53,258 --> 00:11:01,188
She doesn't appreciate my fatherhood, but
she is my heart.

83
00:11:03,883 --> 00:11:09,213
I want life for my daughter and
death for Osman...

84
00:11:10,423 --> 00:11:14,473
from my Allah.

85
00:11:17,299 --> 00:11:22,409
I am waiting with my arms folded...

86
00:11:23,150 --> 00:11:28,000
I can't do anything for both of them.

87
00:11:44,996 --> 00:11:48,266
Don't blame yourself, my Bey.

88
00:11:48,344 --> 00:11:49,884
Don't.

89
00:11:53,507 --> 00:11:58,147
Wait. Wait.

90
00:12:14,636 --> 00:12:18,876
You are right, Hatun.
You are right.

91
00:12:21,824 --> 00:12:23,954
We are going to wait.

92
00:12:31,785 --> 00:12:36,645
We will hear Osman's death.

93
00:12:37,128 --> 00:12:42,868
And I am going to be the Bey.

94
00:12:48,015 --> 00:12:52,805
We are going to wait.
We are going to wait.

95
00:12:53,576 --> 00:12:55,696
We are going to wait.

96
00:12:58,060 --> 00:12:59,990
Wait!

97
00:13:08,924 --> 00:13:11,834
Now open!
Stab!

98
00:13:18,337 --> 00:13:20,837
Stab!
Don't stop!

99
00:13:35,806 --> 00:13:38,266
Now open up!
Stab!

100
00:13:46,780 --> 00:13:48,620
Close up!

101
00:14:07,543 --> 00:14:11,013
Open up!
Stab!

102
00:14:15,609 --> 00:14:17,679
Close up!

103
00:14:40,522 --> 00:14:42,722
Hold on valiants!

104
00:15:31,320 --> 00:15:34,180
Open up!
Stab!

105
00:15:34,584 --> 00:15:36,684
Close up!

106
00:15:39,073 --> 00:15:41,413
Hold on!

107
00:16:52,086 --> 00:16:53,716
Alps!

108
00:16:57,070 --> 00:16:59,300
We retreat!

109
00:16:59,797 --> 00:17:03,067
Retreat!
Now!

110
00:17:06,577 --> 00:17:09,067
Retreat!

111
00:17:11,659 --> 00:17:15,219
Retreat!
Retreat!

112
00:17:19,242 --> 00:17:21,252
Retreat!

113
00:17:45,225 --> 00:17:48,905
- Don't let them escape!
- Retreat!

114
00:17:49,253 --> 00:17:50,983
Forward!

115
00:18:34,932 --> 00:18:37,412
This way, my Bey.

116
00:18:40,025 --> 00:18:43,283
Hold on son.

117
00:18:43,283 --> 00:18:44,993
Hold on my lion!

118
00:18:50,235 --> 00:18:55,865
We are close!
Alps, hold on tight!

119
00:18:56,537 --> 00:19:00,377
Come on my lion!
Come on my lion!

120
00:19:04,365 --> 00:19:07,695
Hold on my valiant!
I'm here!

121
00:19:08,340 --> 00:19:10,200
Hold on my valiant!

122
00:19:13,745 --> 00:19:18,565
Hold tight.
Get the other woundeds!

123
00:19:18,570 --> 00:19:21,490
Hold on my valiant!

124
00:19:22,556 --> 00:19:24,446
Hold on!

125
00:19:44,363 --> 00:19:46,653
Hold on son!

126
00:19:48,898 --> 00:19:51,018
Careful here!

127
00:20:19,563 --> 00:20:21,473
Hold on son.

128
00:20:35,922 --> 00:20:37,642
Go!

129
00:20:44,353 --> 00:20:47,113
Easy, easy.

130
00:20:58,799 --> 00:21:00,379
Come on.

131
00:21:01,733 --> 00:21:03,783
Come on Alps.

132
00:21:11,444 --> 00:21:13,344
Come on Alps!

133
00:21:27,478 --> 00:21:29,258
Let's go!

134
00:22:16,705 --> 00:22:19,035
Shields!

135
00:22:52,211 --> 00:22:58,821
Get out of the way, soldier!
Why are you standing? Go forward, soldier!

136
00:22:59,915 --> 00:23:01,846
Don't let them escape.

137
00:23:01,846 --> 00:23:04,881
They keep the passage!
There are archers, we can't get through!

138
00:23:04,881 --> 00:23:10,811
Osman! You can't escape this time!
Soldier, clear the way!

139
00:23:58,797 --> 00:24:01,987
- Passage is open!
- Soldier!

140
00:24:49,266 --> 00:24:52,126
Get out of my way, soldier!

141
00:24:55,192 --> 00:24:57,681
They have archers, we can't get in.

142
00:24:57,681 --> 00:25:00,278
Osman! Damn it!

143
00:25:00,278 --> 00:25:05,115
Nicola, we can't let him run away. He lost
most of his Alps. He can't deal with us now

144
00:25:05,115 --> 00:25:06,935
Let me finish this.

145
00:25:06,935 --> 00:25:12,139
Let Osman suffer from the defeat.
You shall enjoy your victory, Flatyos.

146
00:25:12,139 --> 00:25:17,509
Nicola, I want to serve you wine in Osman's
skull when you come back from Constantine.

147
00:25:17,591 --> 00:25:23,991
My saint friend, Rome was not found in one
day. Do not let your victory be a defeat.

148
00:25:24,000 --> 00:25:26,690
Enjoy the vengeance of your father.

149
00:25:27,743 --> 00:25:32,003
Soldier, bring me fire!

150
00:25:36,377 --> 00:25:41,397
Take the documents from Göktuğ.
Then kill him.

151
00:25:41,400 --> 00:25:45,500
Also find the betrayer in the castle
before I arrive.

152
00:25:45,611 --> 00:25:48,051
Don't worry, Nicola.

153
00:25:53,024 --> 00:25:56,394
Come on soldier, come on!

154
00:26:15,072 --> 00:26:18,602
Come on son.
Brother, we are close.

155
00:26:19,764 --> 00:26:21,784
Come here.

156
00:26:29,186 --> 00:26:30,666
Brother, come on.

157
00:26:49,317 --> 00:26:54,327
This was your first war, and it shall not
be the last, inshallah (if Allah permits).

158
00:26:56,240 --> 00:26:58,330
This wound won't kill you.

159
00:26:58,898 --> 00:27:03,828
I will thank to Allah one thousand times
for fighting with you, my Bey!

160
00:27:10,568 --> 00:27:16,218
Osman Bey, we have been entrapped.
We have been betrayed.

161
00:27:16,974 --> 00:27:20,534
My Bey, Nicola knew we'd come.

162
00:27:21,238 --> 00:27:26,338
The penalty for betrayal is fined
by sword.

163
00:27:28,577 --> 00:27:33,447
Anyone's blood, even my father's,
is Halal, my Bey.

164
00:27:37,748 --> 00:27:41,725
- Alps, bring the horses.
- Okay my Bey.

165
00:27:41,725 --> 00:27:45,615
Brother take Aygül and the woundeds to
the tent.

166
00:27:45,730 --> 00:27:50,318
- I am not going back without Flatyos.
- Let me go with you, brother.

167
00:27:50,318 --> 00:27:58,198
Brother, go with them. If I fail,
we can't find the betrayer.

168
00:27:58,704 --> 00:28:01,184
Be careful.

169
00:28:08,857 --> 00:28:14,817
We passed the dirty paths thanks to
our faith!

170
00:28:15,196 --> 00:28:19,906
We know how to set a trap the best!

171
00:28:22,318 --> 00:28:26,968
Our swords shall break if we can't make
the infidels pay!

172
00:28:28,192 --> 00:28:33,382
We swear on our eyes which have
seen treachery.

173
00:28:33,382 --> 00:28:41,262
Our breaths shall be Haram if we can't
shed their blood!

174
00:28:41,908 --> 00:28:44,748
Our breaths shall be Haram!
(if we can't shed blood)

175
00:28:47,669 --> 00:28:51,719
Our breaths shall be Haram!
(if we can't shed blood)

176
00:30:03,709 --> 00:30:06,869
Osman must have sent the woundeds
on horse.

177
00:30:06,951 --> 00:30:09,891
He must have left by foot.

178
00:30:10,250 --> 00:30:15,140
They are few in number.
But he has the best Alps.

179
00:30:16,929 --> 00:30:23,199
Soldier, we split!
I don't accept any mistakes!

180
00:30:54,195 --> 00:30:55,935
Lena.

181
00:30:57,266 --> 00:31:01,136
I know you are worried about Bayhoca.

182
00:31:01,596 --> 00:31:06,486
Do not be. They will come back
safe and sound inshaallah (if Allah permits.)

183
00:31:09,114 --> 00:31:13,944
How can I not be, Bala?

184
00:31:16,766 --> 00:31:20,046
We couldn't enjoy Bayhoca's birth.

185
00:31:21,655 --> 00:31:26,895
When my deceased son was little...

186
00:31:29,256 --> 00:31:32,226
I lost him.

187
00:31:34,906 --> 00:31:41,166
I went dry, couldn't breastfeed
Bayhoca enough.

188
00:31:42,793 --> 00:31:45,863
We used to go to his brother's grave.

189
00:31:46,438 --> 00:31:52,938
Don't, Lena. Bayhoca went there with
his father and his uncle.

190
00:31:53,699 --> 00:31:56,689
He wanted to be a Ghazi.

191
00:31:58,545 --> 00:32:02,495
Our valiants live for holy wars, don't
you know that?

192
00:32:10,545 --> 00:32:13,675
Bayhoca saw himself in his dream
last night.

193
00:32:19,259 --> 00:32:21,299
A little bird.

194
00:32:25,302 --> 00:32:29,072
Little like himself.
Worried.

195
00:32:29,842 --> 00:32:32,139
An impatient bird.

196
00:32:34,064 --> 00:32:37,984
The bird flew off, he said.

197
00:32:57,718 --> 00:33:00,318
Maybe it's not a life bird.

198
00:33:04,684 --> 00:33:08,614
Maybe it was all his problems
that flew off.

199
00:33:12,803 --> 00:33:17,563
The war he went with his father and uncle
took all of his problems away.

200
00:33:21,445 --> 00:33:26,335
Sword in one hand, bridle in the other.

201
00:33:26,798 --> 00:33:29,808
May Allah bless his fight.

202
00:33:32,258 --> 00:33:33,778
Amin.

203
00:33:41,320 --> 00:33:45,270
May Allah grant us with our loved ones.

204
00:33:51,526 --> 00:33:58,256
I knew what it is like to be a Hatun of
an Alp. I was destined to suffer from...

205
00:33:58,952 --> 00:34:01,832
the pain of being an Alp's mother.

206
00:34:13,055 --> 00:34:14,795
I shall leave.

207
00:34:18,621 --> 00:34:21,091
I have things to do.

208
00:34:25,208 --> 00:34:27,138
Of course.

209
00:34:41,105 --> 00:34:47,795
I witnessed my brothers' deaths.
My mother couldn't resist to all the pain.

210
00:34:49,749 --> 00:34:51,689
I feel her.

211
00:34:52,901 --> 00:34:57,801
This land taught us that fear doesn't
change the end.

212
00:35:03,431 --> 00:35:10,161
My Osman Bey will eventually pay both
Nicola and Flatyos.

213
00:35:12,585 --> 00:35:16,475
So Osman Bey and his Alps went to
finish it, huh?

214
00:35:24,071 --> 00:35:27,781
He won't come back before he finishes
this. I know it.

215
00:35:29,684 --> 00:35:31,664
Don't worry.

216
00:35:35,669 --> 00:35:39,989
I am not worried about two ignobles who
Osman Bey is after.

217
00:35:42,781 --> 00:35:49,787
What I am worried about is what Potter
İdris says before he dies.

218
00:35:49,787 --> 00:35:54,847
- Whose dog are you?
- I'll tell you. I'll tell you.

219
00:35:55,187 --> 00:36:01,351
I'll tell you all. The betrayers are
so close to you, Osman Bey.

220
00:36:04,399 --> 00:36:06,769
What do you mean, Hatun?

221
00:36:07,669 --> 00:36:14,119
Like dog İdris said, Osman Bey should have
avoid the nearest enemy.

222
00:36:15,871 --> 00:36:19,671
He should have found the betrayer
in the tent first.

223
00:36:20,092 --> 00:36:24,872
Even his Alps don't know what they
are fighting for, where they are headed.

224
00:36:25,326 --> 00:36:27,686
Don't worry about Osman Bey.

225
00:36:30,036 --> 00:36:36,326
My Father says the ones who we trust the
most teach us to not trust anyone.

226
00:36:36,907 --> 00:36:39,647
What are you trying to say, Malhun Hatun?

227
00:36:42,371 --> 00:36:46,911
There was no one to know we were going to
battle except for his Beys. Don't you hear?

228
00:36:50,589 --> 00:36:55,459
Should he suspect Savcı Bey, or Dündar Bey
whose daughter is in the war?

229
00:36:55,465 --> 00:36:59,045
Or Gündüz Bey who is ready to
sacrifice his life for his brother.

230
00:37:00,508 --> 00:37:03,718
You are talking nonsense.

231
00:37:04,735 --> 00:37:06,795
Bala Hatun.

232
00:37:11,595 --> 00:37:16,555
You are getting angry, but don't you see
that I am worried about Osman Bey?

233
00:37:19,878 --> 00:37:23,418
Osman Bey has been my hope for my people.

234
00:37:23,975 --> 00:37:25,636
I won't let anything bad hap...

235
00:37:25,636 --> 00:37:28,606
Osman Bey is hope for all of us
Malhun Hatun!

236
00:37:29,557 --> 00:37:34,847
He hasn't lost any war he was in so far!
You can stay cool!

237
00:37:35,429 --> 00:37:39,679
I will neither stay cool nor confirm
this land to my father...

238
00:37:39,679 --> 00:37:43,665
unless I find the owner of the arrow
that shot İdris.

239
00:37:47,781 --> 00:37:50,521
I shall leave.

240
00:37:52,094 --> 00:37:56,614
I need to leave you to your coolness.

241
00:38:17,213 --> 00:38:18,873
Good luck with it.

242
00:38:20,256 --> 00:38:25,406
- Take it, have a nice day.
- May Allah bless you.

243
00:39:33,220 --> 00:39:39,900
I always wondered about the dirt that
will come out when I scalp you.

244
00:39:40,513 --> 00:39:45,983
Geyhatu's hunt dog Böke.

245
00:39:47,606 --> 00:39:54,996
How did you find out Kızıl Bey's son Umur
was after us, Petrus? How did you track us?

246
00:39:55,369 --> 00:39:58,279
How did you inform us?

247
00:39:58,527 --> 00:40:05,657
I am responsible for the flying birds,
the running foxes...

248
00:40:05,657 --> 00:40:09,557
the venomous snakes hereabouts.

249
00:40:11,361 --> 00:40:16,521
Just like I know where Umur Bey is.

250
00:40:17,725 --> 00:40:19,695
Where is he?

251
00:40:24,908 --> 00:40:30,908
If Black Shaman Togay agrees with me...

252
00:40:32,032 --> 00:40:36,932
You are going to find out where he is.

253
00:40:41,020 --> 00:40:47,050
Both Togay and I know very well why
Turks are rushing to west.

254
00:40:48,956 --> 00:40:54,896
I know who has the certificate of occupancy
of Osman and Turkmens.

255
00:40:57,432 --> 00:40:59,932
What do you want in return?

256
00:41:00,988 --> 00:41:05,488
- We have a common enemy with Geyhatu.
- Osman.

257
00:41:07,632 --> 00:41:14,462
I will give Umur Bey's tent to Togay
in return of Osman's head.

258
00:42:26,846 --> 00:42:28,446
No.

259
00:43:18,561 --> 00:43:20,771
Nephew!

260
00:43:35,833 --> 00:43:37,763
No!

261
00:43:40,715 --> 00:43:43,055
No!

262
00:43:43,826 --> 00:43:46,126
No!

263
00:43:59,506 --> 00:44:01,416
Bayhoca!

264
00:44:01,813 --> 00:44:06,300
Hold on Ghazi! I want something from you.
Do not die!

265
00:44:06,300 --> 00:44:08,200
Do not die!

266
00:44:08,855 --> 00:44:11,975
- Bayhoca!
- Brother, what happened?

267
00:44:11,975 --> 00:44:14,155
I'll tell you later, brother.

268
00:44:17,263 --> 00:44:22,063
- No, no, no!
- Easy!

269
00:44:24,118 --> 00:44:26,138
Bayhoca!

270
00:44:28,185 --> 00:44:30,240
No no no!

271
00:44:30,240 --> 00:44:33,100
Lena!
Lena!

272
00:44:39,959 --> 00:44:41,739
Move!

273
00:44:44,226 --> 00:44:46,730
You can't leave us.

274
00:44:46,730 --> 00:44:48,520
Lena!

275
00:44:49,821 --> 00:44:53,231
Move! Help Alps!

276
00:44:53,393 --> 00:44:59,031
Get the care tent ready immediately!
Take the wounded alps there!

277
00:44:59,031 --> 00:45:01,731
Pull yourself together!

278
00:45:02,101 --> 00:45:04,511
Hold on!

279
00:45:06,150 --> 00:45:08,420
Osman is absent.

280
00:45:15,372 --> 00:45:18,912
Thank Allah, Aygül is back.

281
00:45:20,593 --> 00:45:24,533
- Mother, I will be gone.
- No no!

282
00:45:25,871 --> 00:45:29,551
No you can't leave us!

283
00:45:29,582 --> 00:45:32,701
Let's carry him!

284
00:45:32,701 --> 00:45:35,781
Come on Alps!
Carry the woundeds!

285
00:45:36,993 --> 00:45:38,913
Hold on son!

286
00:45:43,358 --> 00:45:47,288
Hatuns! Let's get the care tent ready!

287
00:45:47,966 --> 00:45:49,684
- Don't shake him!

288
00:45:49,684 --> 00:45:52,227
Get the care tent ready!

289
00:45:52,227 --> 00:45:56,435
- Hold on nephew!
- Clear the way!

290
00:45:56,435 --> 00:46:00,155
I won't leave you Bayhoca!

291
00:46:01,455 --> 00:46:08,715
- I won't leave you Bayhoca!
- Hold on nephew!

292
00:46:15,165 --> 00:46:20,639
What are you waiting for, Dündar Bey.
Go help the woundeds.

293
00:46:34,258 --> 00:46:38,388
Bring clear cloth!
Gonca! Gonca.

294
00:46:51,189 --> 00:46:55,080
Compress the wound with the cloth Gonca.

295
00:46:55,080 --> 00:46:57,008
- Hold on.
- Inshallah.

296
00:46:57,008 --> 00:47:00,618
Bring it at once!
I'll brand the wound!

297
00:47:09,808 --> 00:47:12,378
How did you got ambushed?

298
00:47:13,594 --> 00:47:16,534
They knew that we were coming.

299
00:47:26,806 --> 00:47:29,456
Come on, come on!

300
00:47:43,980 --> 00:47:48,930
His bleeding won't stop, his bleeding
won't stop Savcı!

301
00:47:55,270 --> 00:47:58,670
Open your eyes, please
Don't close your eyes!

302
00:48:00,848 --> 00:48:04,748
Son, hold on, son.

303
00:48:06,252 --> 00:48:12,312
Hold on my valiant! Open your eyes,
don't leave us like that son!

304
00:48:12,729 --> 00:48:17,369
- Baysungur, tell me what happened?
- My Bey, Nicola knew everything.

305
00:48:19,193 --> 00:48:22,733
We got ambushed, they shot Bayhoca.

306
00:48:28,098 --> 00:48:32,458
What happened? Where is the rest?
Where is Osman?

307
00:48:34,264 --> 00:48:36,324
We got ambushed.

308
00:48:38,740 --> 00:48:43,160
We have martyreds.
And woundeds.

309
00:48:43,646 --> 00:48:47,756
Osman Bey went after Flatyos with
a bunch of alps.

310
00:49:04,793 --> 00:49:09,713
I told you! The betrayer is so close! They
know everything about Osman Bey's plan.

311
00:49:09,779 --> 00:49:15,949
Hatun! This not the right time!
Are you going to help or what?

312
00:50:21,658 --> 00:50:25,308
How did you know we were going to
got ambushed, Göktuğ?

313
00:50:25,308 --> 00:50:26,648
Zülfikar.

314
00:50:34,228 --> 00:50:37,498
May God protect our soldiers.
Amen.

315
00:50:38,042 --> 00:50:42,412
May God grant Lord Nicola with victory
on his ambush against Osman.

316
00:50:42,412 --> 00:50:44,232
Amen.

317
00:50:46,451 --> 00:50:49,261
I have to get to Osman Bey.

318
00:50:50,905 --> 00:50:53,515
Zülfikar Dervish ha?

319
00:50:54,250 --> 00:50:58,060
Valiant Zülfikar.
He shall live long.

320
00:50:59,504 --> 00:51:02,374
Now they will be in the middle of the
ambush.

321
00:51:02,670 --> 00:51:08,800
Leave Flatyos to me.
He'll give me the betrayer in the tent.

322
00:51:10,465 --> 00:51:12,965
Wait for my sign.

323
00:51:29,515 --> 00:51:31,895
Alps!

324
00:51:49,148 --> 00:51:51,808
Flatyos.

325
00:51:56,537 --> 00:51:59,827
Do you think I will surrender, Osman Bey?

326
00:51:59,940 --> 00:52:06,070
I knew I'd entrap you like the back of
my hand.

327
00:52:11,297 --> 00:52:14,997
To death, then.

328
00:52:16,502 --> 00:52:18,452
Let's begin.

329
00:53:44,798 --> 00:53:47,718
Go on, finish it Osman Bey.

330
00:53:50,701 --> 00:53:53,131
I told you.

331
00:53:56,132 --> 00:53:59,362
Your won't go easily.

332
00:54:04,963 --> 00:54:10,733
You'll tell me everything until your
tongue goes rotten.

333
00:54:15,787 --> 00:54:21,288
How did Cumans get in our tent?

334
00:54:21,288 --> 00:54:26,858
You get in and out of our castle
constantly, and now this is what you say?

335
00:54:47,110 --> 00:54:48,520
Tell me.

336
00:54:52,070 --> 00:54:55,000
Who did the potter serve to?

337
00:55:05,721 --> 00:55:11,791
Who told you about my plan for Nicola?

338
00:55:14,555 --> 00:55:17,015
Who, ha? Who!

339
00:55:18,643 --> 00:55:22,133
Every community has betrayers inside,
Osman Bey.

340
00:55:30,174 --> 00:55:34,854
He doesn't have the face to come back,
Hatun.

341
00:55:34,854 --> 00:55:38,632
He is trying to convert the defeat
to victory.

342
00:55:38,632 --> 00:55:44,252
He'll die so that he can show everyone
he won and got his revenge.

343
00:55:48,439 --> 00:55:51,679
It was obvious that his greed would
drag him down.

344
00:55:52,390 --> 00:56:01,010
Inshallah he can't come back so that other
Alps can live.

345
00:56:01,698 --> 00:56:07,196
He won't be able to come back, Hatun.

346
00:56:07,196 --> 00:56:12,366
Don't you see his Alps, they are
exhausted. He can't get Flatyos.

347
00:56:13,129 --> 00:56:16,499
He won't be able to come back.
He won't be able to come back.

348
00:56:31,770 --> 00:56:38,080
Alps!
Take him to the tent.

349
00:56:39,335 --> 00:56:44,855
I'll make him talk before he breaths
for the last time.

350
00:56:45,750 --> 00:56:47,520
Go.

351
00:57:05,837 --> 00:57:07,627
Brother.

352
00:57:12,754 --> 00:57:15,344
One last duty is waiting for you.

353
00:57:15,344 --> 00:57:19,499
I know my Bey. They'll come to get
the certificate of occupancy.

354
00:57:19,499 --> 00:57:22,832
I'll learn who are the spies of Papa,
who cooperates with Nicola.

355
00:57:22,832 --> 00:57:28,732
If you can succeed, we will find out who
the betrayer is in the tribe.

356
00:57:29,874 --> 00:57:33,534
- May Allah help you.
- Eyvallah(thank you) my Bey

357
00:57:37,575 --> 00:57:39,455
Let's move!

358
00:57:57,954 --> 00:58:03,524
Open your eyes son!
Don't leave us alone!

359
00:58:06,242 --> 00:58:07,572
Father!

360
00:58:12,781 --> 00:58:15,241
Where is my sword?

361
00:58:17,194 --> 00:58:20,294
I'll fetch it son!

362
00:58:20,975 --> 00:58:24,945
No, Bayhoca! Don't leave!

363
00:58:24,972 --> 00:58:27,345
- Son! Son!
- Open your eyes!

364
00:58:27,345 --> 00:58:32,425
Here is your sword son!
Open your eyes!

365
00:58:36,483 --> 00:58:39,862
Give me your blessings.

366
00:58:39,862 --> 00:58:43,490
Don't son! Don't!
Open your eyes!

367
00:58:43,490 --> 00:58:46,770
Hold on my valiant!

368
00:58:46,779 --> 00:58:49,477
Don't leave us Bayhoca!

369
00:58:49,477 --> 00:58:52,707
Being a Ghazi...

370
00:58:52,890 --> 00:58:57,240
- You can't leave!
- Shahada...

371
00:58:58,302 --> 00:59:00,452
You can't leave!

372
00:59:02,665 --> 00:59:07,625
I bear witness that there is no deity
but Allah...

373
00:59:10,307 --> 00:59:18,437
and I bear witness that Muhammad is the
messenger of Allah.

374
00:59:42,849 --> 00:59:47,529
No, no, no, Bayhoca!

375
00:59:47,562 --> 00:59:51,352
Bayhoca open your eyes!
Open your eyes!

376
00:59:51,723 --> 00:59:54,893
No, no!
Open your eyes!

377
00:59:56,165 --> 00:59:58,887
Bayhoca open your eyes!

378
00:59:58,887 --> 01:00:06,110
Please don't leave us!
Open your eyes!

379
01:00:06,110 --> 01:00:10,650
Open your eyes Bayhoca!
Open your eyes!

380
01:00:18,044 --> 01:00:20,884
Open your eyes!

381
01:00:23,021 --> 01:00:25,367
Bayhoca open your eyes!

382
01:00:25,367 --> 01:00:28,347
Please don't leave us alone!

383
01:00:36,382 --> 01:00:39,002
Open your eyes!

384
01:00:45,408 --> 01:00:48,018
Open your eyes Bayhoca!

385
01:00:57,007 --> 01:01:03,407
Open your eyes Bayhoca!
Open your eyes my son, please!

386
01:01:56,850 --> 01:02:00,130
How can you do it, Savcı?

387
01:02:03,178 --> 01:02:07,708
How can you clothe him?

388
01:02:23,585 --> 01:02:27,725
He is in Jannah, Hatun.
Don't cry anymore.

389
01:02:46,463 --> 01:02:51,373
Why did you take him to the
battle, Savcı?

390
01:02:52,169 --> 01:02:55,069
Why did you?

391
01:02:59,518 --> 01:03:02,648
Oh Bayhoca...

392
01:03:49,190 --> 01:03:51,460
Bayhoca...

393
01:04:10,790 --> 01:04:13,760
The good ones live less, Lena.

394
01:04:24,080 --> 01:04:26,480
Valiants go first.

395
01:04:58,711 --> 01:05:04,551
Bayhoca...
No, no, no!

396
01:05:06,262 --> 01:05:09,512
He deceased with no sin, Lena.

397
01:05:09,664 --> 01:05:11,335
No, no!

398
01:05:11,335 --> 01:05:14,675
He died before the world dirt him.

399
01:05:16,596 --> 01:05:19,966
No, no...

400
01:05:21,862 --> 01:05:26,952
I know this pain the best, my nephew.

401
01:05:29,214 --> 01:05:32,484
There's nothing else to do then
being patient.

402
01:05:33,628 --> 01:05:35,238
There is not.

403
01:05:49,756 --> 01:05:51,936
He was a brave valiant.

404
01:05:55,019 --> 01:05:57,879
He must be in Jannah now.

405
01:06:02,695 --> 01:06:06,115
Bayhoca...

406
01:06:34,274 --> 01:06:36,774
Bayhoca...

407
01:06:37,208 --> 01:06:41,058
Get up, my child get up...

408
01:06:43,731 --> 01:06:45,841
Please...

409
01:07:07,818 --> 01:07:12,198
What is it, uncle?
Where are you headed?

410
01:07:13,623 --> 01:07:15,633
Osman.

411
01:07:18,372 --> 01:07:20,712
You are back, huh?

412
01:07:22,827 --> 01:07:25,357
We were worried about you.

413
01:07:27,090 --> 01:07:32,310
We got ambushed.
We killed the infidels, inshallah.

414
01:07:34,605 --> 01:07:39,315
I know, I know, Masha Allah (praise be)

415
01:07:41,522 --> 01:07:42,962
And Flatyos...

416
01:07:48,675 --> 01:07:51,715
Bala.

417
01:08:15,232 --> 01:08:17,152
Bala.

418
01:08:56,185 --> 01:08:59,985
Who is this martyr lying down in
my tent?

419
01:11:26,182 --> 01:11:32,342
I failed, brother, I failed.

420
01:11:36,257 --> 01:11:38,847
I couldn't protect him.

421
01:11:43,894 --> 01:11:48,784
He slipped through my hands.

422
01:11:53,759 --> 01:11:56,319
He's gone.

423
01:12:09,241 --> 01:12:12,981
He flew off like a little bird.

424
01:12:14,654 --> 01:12:16,974
Oh Bayhoca.

425
01:12:31,681 --> 01:12:34,011
Oh, my nephew.

426
01:12:36,770 --> 01:12:39,170
You wanted to be a Ghazi.

427
01:12:43,039 --> 01:12:46,349
You fought in the middle.

428
01:12:50,041 --> 01:12:52,841
But you are a martyr now.

429
01:12:57,531 --> 01:13:02,711
You are a martyr now.
A martyr.

430
01:13:06,645 --> 01:13:08,985
You are in Jannah.

431
01:13:15,918 --> 01:13:17,888
But...

432
01:13:18,522 --> 01:13:21,482
but you burned your uncle's heart.

433
01:13:32,094 --> 01:13:34,704
Help me, brother.

434
01:13:37,688 --> 01:13:42,628
Help me find that dog.

435
01:13:44,499 --> 01:13:48,419
I won't relieve until I kill him.

436
01:13:49,844 --> 01:13:51,844
Brother.

437
01:13:55,485 --> 01:13:59,295
Did you think I'd come here without
that dog?

438
01:14:18,158 --> 01:14:20,578
Do you have him brother?

439
01:14:22,101 --> 01:14:24,511
I do.

440
01:14:34,007 --> 01:14:37,107
- So, you have him.
- I do.

441
01:14:40,447 --> 01:14:42,937
Flatyos is here.

442
01:15:22,967 --> 01:15:25,537
I will kill him.

443
01:15:29,352 --> 01:15:31,831
- Lena.
- I'll kill him! Let go of me!

444
01:15:31,831 --> 01:15:35,441
Lena!
Bala, stay here.

445
01:15:49,362 --> 01:15:52,432
Osman brought Flatyos to make him talk.

446
01:15:54,787 --> 01:15:58,667
Osman brought Flatyos to make him talk.

447
01:16:01,957 --> 01:16:04,317
If he speaks...

448
01:16:05,868 --> 01:16:11,178
If he speaks, then be ready for anything,
Hatun.

449
01:16:12,600 --> 01:16:14,850
We may need to run away.

450
01:16:17,588 --> 01:16:19,378
Run away?

451
01:16:19,476 --> 01:16:24,536
To where are we going to run away
Dündar Bey?!

452
01:16:29,013 --> 01:16:33,513
If Flatyos speaks...

453
01:16:34,423 --> 01:16:38,943
Don't let someone else kill me, Dündar Bey.

454
01:16:38,964 --> 01:16:43,674
You should kill me.

455
01:16:43,863 --> 01:16:50,013
What are you talking about Hatun? If things
come to that, why would I kill you?

456
01:16:52,943 --> 01:16:55,423
There are a lot of men to kill.

457
01:17:02,206 --> 01:17:06,746
Then kill him.

458
01:17:07,774 --> 01:17:12,704
Or make someone do it.

459
01:17:33,843 --> 01:17:35,923
Here we go again.

460
01:17:43,068 --> 01:17:46,258
For how long do you think you'll keep me.

461
01:17:47,238 --> 01:17:51,598
My Bey already told you, until your
tongue goes rotten.

462
01:17:52,726 --> 01:17:55,736
The previous visit of mine was short.

463
01:17:56,650 --> 01:18:00,780
We'll see if you can run away when
your legs are broken.

464
01:18:05,827 --> 01:18:08,787
Bamsi Bey is here as well.

465
01:18:09,582 --> 01:18:12,882
Of course he wouldn't miss the show.

466
01:18:14,960 --> 01:18:18,340
Flatyos... Flatyos...

467
01:18:19,437 --> 01:18:27,021
Where are you going to go before we make
pay for the Alps and Suleiman Shah's

468
01:18:27,021 --> 01:18:30,205
beloved one Bayhoca.

469
01:18:30,205 --> 01:18:32,895
Is it only Bayhoca, Bamsı Bey?

470
01:18:32,933 --> 01:18:37,683
Remember Dumrul who I riddled with holes,
Ayaz whose stomach I slit.

471
01:18:37,951 --> 01:18:41,141
Do you want me to count more?

472
01:18:47,389 --> 01:18:55,909
My Allah shall witness me, I won't die
before I smell your dead body.

473
01:18:58,861 --> 01:19:00,721
Stop, daughter.

474
01:19:03,330 --> 01:19:06,950
Bamsi Bey.
Let me.

475
01:19:08,150 --> 01:19:11,620
Let me spit on my son's killer's face.

476
01:19:17,812 --> 01:19:19,802
Let me.

477
01:19:34,248 --> 01:19:40,128
You didn't give me your love, but
you gave your son, Lena.

478
01:19:49,284 --> 01:19:52,034
- Die!
- Stop, aunt.

479
01:19:57,783 --> 01:19:59,973
Stop.

480
01:20:06,461 --> 01:20:09,841
In order not to let more mothers cry...

481
01:20:13,526 --> 01:20:16,216
I must make this dog talk.

482
01:20:31,736 --> 01:20:33,536
Let go.

483
01:20:35,325 --> 01:20:39,935
If you let my son down before he
goes into the grave...

484
01:20:41,919 --> 01:20:44,569
I won't give you my blessings, Osman Bey.

485
01:21:26,896 --> 01:21:31,176
- Tell me what happened.
- We lost Commander Flatyos.

486
01:21:34,522 --> 01:21:36,412
How can it be?

487
01:21:36,973 --> 01:21:40,523
How did this happen?

488
01:21:41,005 --> 01:21:43,645
Göktuğ attacked us with Cumans.

489
01:21:43,704 --> 01:21:45,564
Göktuğ?

490
01:21:47,827 --> 01:21:50,437
I should have seen that!

491
01:21:51,129 --> 01:21:55,179
I should have seen that damn it!

492
01:21:57,738 --> 01:22:02,918
Soldier, inform Constantinople.
Now!

493
01:22:05,663 --> 01:22:08,113
Flatyos!

494
01:22:08,822 --> 01:22:11,302
Flatyos!

495
01:22:17,288 --> 01:22:21,248
There are a lot of betrayers in your
tribe, Osman.

496
01:22:25,714 --> 01:22:27,914
Talk.

497
01:22:29,209 --> 01:22:34,459
Talk so you die in the easy way.

498
01:22:40,594 --> 01:22:43,084
I always wanted the hard way, Osman.

499
01:22:46,633 --> 01:22:48,763
To kill your father.

500
01:23:04,807 --> 01:23:06,597
I wanted Lena.

501
01:23:13,603 --> 01:23:16,583
I know the potter is not alone here.

502
01:23:17,233 --> 01:23:20,893
Who is the other betrayer?
Talk!

503
01:23:21,481 --> 01:23:23,551
Who?

504
01:23:23,889 --> 01:23:25,469
Tell me!

505
01:23:28,041 --> 01:23:33,651
Potter's soul came to finish his
uncomplete job, Osman.

506
01:23:46,031 --> 01:23:48,811
Who are Papa's spies?

507
01:23:50,226 --> 01:23:53,466
Who did Nicola ally with?

508
01:23:54,597 --> 01:23:57,467
With whom?!

509
01:24:06,457 --> 01:24:12,297
So many enemies you have, Osman.
Nicola was confused to choose.

510
01:24:14,711 --> 01:24:17,335
You were lucky today, Osman.

511
01:24:17,335 --> 01:24:19,715
But this will not last long.

512
01:24:22,087 --> 01:24:26,137
Nicola will capture you now or later.

513
01:24:51,158 --> 01:24:52,648
Brother.

514
01:24:55,681 --> 01:24:58,071
His yours.

515
01:24:58,448 --> 01:24:59,948
Yours.

516
01:25:04,789 --> 01:25:08,499
Do you know why I aimed for Bayhoca,
Savcı Bey?

517
01:25:08,561 --> 01:25:12,481
Who is the betrayer that told
we were after Nicola.

518
01:25:12,498 --> 01:25:15,558
Because you took my love.

519
01:25:17,302 --> 01:25:20,122
And I took your son.

520
01:25:46,282 --> 01:25:53,152
Beys, I prefer cutting my tongue to speak!

521
01:26:05,339 --> 01:26:07,239
Boran1

522
01:26:14,577 --> 01:26:18,797
Osman Bey! This dog won't speak.

523
01:26:19,618 --> 01:26:24,275
Each breath of his will create chaos.
Kill him.

524
01:26:24,275 --> 01:26:31,345
Uncle! Many Alps' blood is in this
dog's hand.

525
01:26:32,146 --> 01:26:36,056
Don't say it again.

526
01:26:38,349 --> 01:26:45,889
This one won't die until he speaks.

527
01:26:52,316 --> 01:26:56,036
Brother, until his last breathe...

528
01:27:00,220 --> 01:27:03,740
he'll tell us everything he knows.

529
01:27:30,466 --> 01:27:34,164
I am telling you, the betrayer is not far,
they are right near you.

530
01:27:34,164 --> 01:27:38,454
Watch your mouth, Hatun.
Just tell who you are accusing.

531
01:27:40,616 --> 01:27:44,046
You are in pain.

532
01:27:45,446 --> 01:27:50,566
You can't see things.
I'll reveal it.

533
01:27:55,140 --> 01:27:57,710
What are you going to reveal?

534
01:27:59,306 --> 01:28:02,506
Are you here to create chaos, Hatun?

535
01:28:04,557 --> 01:28:07,047
What is your problem?

536
01:28:08,008 --> 01:28:12,948
Bala Hatun, let go of my arm first.

537
01:28:20,116 --> 01:28:24,056
No need to create chaos in this tent.

538
01:28:25,568 --> 01:28:28,468
There's chaos and treachery in every
corner.

539
01:28:28,961 --> 01:28:31,421
Don't you see it?

540
01:28:44,565 --> 01:28:47,165
He can't die...

541
01:28:50,150 --> 01:28:52,540
He can't die...

542
01:29:07,742 --> 01:29:10,322
Why is he still alive?

543
01:29:21,176 --> 01:29:24,456
Why aren't you still keeping him alive,
Savcı?

544
01:29:28,754 --> 01:29:30,934
He'll die, Hatun.

545
01:29:33,263 --> 01:29:35,693
He'll die.

546
01:29:37,612 --> 01:29:41,262
In the most fearful way.

547
01:29:43,200 --> 01:29:46,090
He can't get away with this.

548
01:29:46,690 --> 01:29:53,070
Each breath he takes flare up the
fire in my heart.

549
01:30:11,320 --> 01:30:19,000
Why Osman Bey doesn't want us to take
revenge, kill the murderer of our son?

550
01:30:21,966 --> 01:30:24,376
How can I live with it?

551
01:30:28,545 --> 01:30:31,125
How can my heart bear up?

552
01:30:34,327 --> 01:30:37,127
Do you think I am not in pain, Hatun?

553
01:30:46,840 --> 01:30:53,370
Do you think it was easy to see him dying,
Hatun?

554
01:30:56,839 --> 01:30:58,759
But...

555
01:31:00,875 --> 01:31:03,985
We have to find the betrayer in the tribe.

556
01:31:03,989 --> 01:31:08,169
- We don't have to!
- Lena

557
01:31:08,763 --> 01:31:11,492
- Lena...
- We don't have to, Savcı Bey.

558
01:31:11,492 --> 01:31:14,012
- Lena.
- Kill him.

559
01:31:14,329 --> 01:31:16,189
Savcı Bey ki...

560
01:31:16,688 --> 01:31:19,828
Lena!

561
01:31:20,557 --> 01:31:24,987
Be calm, Hatun.
Be calm, Hatun.

562
01:31:26,318 --> 01:31:31,398
Keep calm, my Lena.
Keep calm.

563
01:31:31,398 --> 01:31:35,698
- Keep calm.
- Savcı Bey.

564
01:31:36,411 --> 01:31:38,711
Kill him!

565
01:31:40,636 --> 01:31:42,346
Kill!

566
01:32:16,566 --> 01:32:19,526
Don't want him from me, brother.

567
01:32:21,576 --> 01:32:23,826
Don't.

568
01:32:27,259 --> 01:32:29,259
Osman.

569
01:32:29,634 --> 01:32:35,084
Brother...
I can't look at Lena's face.

570
01:32:36,688 --> 01:32:40,698
Come on, Flatyos won't talk.

571
01:32:40,787 --> 01:32:45,687
He will, brother.
He will.

572
01:32:47,091 --> 01:32:51,821
Now or later, I'll make him talk.

573
01:32:51,963 --> 01:32:56,833
It'll take months, brother.
My Hatun is pregnant.

574
01:32:56,835 --> 01:33:00,235
She can't do it while Flatyos is here.

575
01:33:00,658 --> 01:33:04,748
Let me take the revenge of my child.

576
01:33:11,820 --> 01:33:18,540
Brother, your pain is my pain.

577
01:33:19,999 --> 01:33:24,709
Your lament is my lament brother.

578
01:33:26,525 --> 01:33:31,675
He is your son, my nephew.

579
01:33:35,336 --> 01:33:41,256
I know how unbearable this pain is.

580
01:33:42,606 --> 01:33:48,996
However, you should feel me too.

581
01:33:50,799 --> 01:33:55,519
Let me take revenge of my son before
he kills my unborn child too.

582
01:33:56,525 --> 01:34:01,295
Brother, tell my aunt that...

583
01:34:02,692 --> 01:34:09,572
Osman will kill Flatyos in every breath
he takes, slowly.

584
01:34:11,395 --> 01:34:17,125
Killing Flatyos for once is a gift
for him.

585
01:34:18,399 --> 01:34:23,969
Don't break us one more time, Osman.
Let me finish this.

586
01:34:24,244 --> 01:34:28,974
Go, brother.
Go away.

587
01:34:32,750 --> 01:34:35,600
Let's not make our pain stronger.

588
01:34:37,161 --> 01:34:42,171
Go away from my presence before

589
01:34:43,746 --> 01:34:46,436
we fall out with each other.

590
01:35:21,978 --> 01:35:24,178
My valiant father.

591
01:35:30,239 --> 01:35:33,409
You taught me how to be like
a lion in the war and...

592
01:35:35,155 --> 01:35:41,435
how to be calm in peace.

593
01:35:43,718 --> 01:35:47,508
I sacrifice my head in your way, father.

594
01:35:49,658 --> 01:35:54,168
But, show me a way out now.

595
01:35:57,316 --> 01:36:00,466
Show me a way, my Ghazi father.

596
01:36:08,430 --> 01:36:13,650
How hard it is to be a Bey...

597
01:36:16,640 --> 01:36:18,950
in all these treacheries...

598
01:36:23,651 --> 01:36:26,391
in all this pain.

599
01:36:40,354 --> 01:36:42,754
Can I, nephew?

600
01:36:47,282 --> 01:36:49,362
Come uncle.

601
01:37:06,323 --> 01:37:11,413
Osman Bey doesn't let you, does he?

602
01:37:19,804 --> 01:37:22,404
I know how painful losing a child is.

603
01:37:23,564 --> 01:37:29,604
That pain burns your heart.

604
01:37:30,612 --> 01:37:32,672
I know it.

605
01:37:35,378 --> 01:37:38,868
Osman Bey is also right, uncle.

606
01:37:41,011 --> 01:37:47,241
We have to make Flatyus talk to
find out the betrayer.

607
01:37:49,251 --> 01:37:55,041
Do you think he'll talk?
That snake will not talk.

608
01:37:55,684 --> 01:38:03,564
Whoever that ignoble dog betrayed us will
capture him from the tent!

609
01:38:03,911 --> 01:38:06,011
I will choke him!

610
01:38:07,288 --> 01:38:10,518
Of course you will.

611
01:38:12,933 --> 01:38:15,803
You have the right.

612
01:38:16,860 --> 01:38:22,990
You have the right to kill him.

613
01:38:23,713 --> 01:38:28,613
I support you nephew, I support you.

614
01:38:28,784 --> 01:38:33,814
Uncle, let me think.

615
01:38:36,394 --> 01:38:39,014
Let me think.

616
01:38:50,683 --> 01:38:53,900
She comes and goes around,
she provokes me.

617
01:38:53,900 --> 01:38:56,020
What does she say, Hatun?

618
01:38:56,587 --> 01:38:58,247
What does she say?

619
01:38:58,564 --> 01:39:00,714
How does she provoke you?

620
01:39:01,386 --> 01:39:06,247
She says there are betrayers among us
They are so close to us but we don't see.

621
01:39:06,247 --> 01:39:08,167
She is right.

622
01:39:11,350 --> 01:39:15,720
There's a betrayer among us and he is
so close to us.

623
01:39:17,253 --> 01:39:21,193
Is it Malhun Hatun's job to reveal
him, Osman?

624
01:39:30,401 --> 01:39:35,241
We have been betrayed, we should
find him.

625
01:39:36,455 --> 01:39:41,875
No one can involve in our issues
and make us feel small!

626
01:39:45,559 --> 01:39:50,599
My Bala, my heart burns.

627
01:39:50,865 --> 01:39:53,675
My heart burns.

628
01:39:54,555 --> 01:39:58,785
I can barely stand not to kill
that Flatyos.

629
01:40:02,317 --> 01:40:08,137
Do not push me.

630
01:40:32,054 --> 01:40:34,714
Forgive me my Osman.

631
01:40:36,601 --> 01:40:44,681
Until I kill that dog, I am not me.

632
01:40:49,843 --> 01:40:51,453
I am..

633
01:40:54,448 --> 01:40:57,058
not me, Hatun.

634
01:41:09,743 --> 01:41:12,803
Wait for my heart to cool off.

635
01:41:58,351 --> 01:42:00,311
Get out.

636
01:42:11,302 --> 01:42:16,572
My Bey, don't.
Osman Bey has a certain command.

637
01:42:22,079 --> 01:42:24,489
Let Lena Hatun out, my Bey.

638
01:42:25,625 --> 01:42:30,204
- Don't do it please.
- Osman Bey wanted me to make him talk.

639
01:42:30,204 --> 01:42:33,474
Baysungur, get away.

640
01:42:39,728 --> 01:42:43,288
- My Bey, don't.
- Baysungur! Move!

641
01:43:37,587 --> 01:43:40,217
This is the last time I'm asking.

642
01:43:41,304 --> 01:43:43,964
Who is the betrayer?

643
01:43:44,338 --> 01:43:49,143
You'll live with the hole I dig
in your heart forever.

644
01:43:49,143 --> 01:43:54,133
I won't die as long as you die.

645
01:43:56,220 --> 01:44:01,650
In each breath, every time you remember
your son...

646
01:44:03,924 --> 01:44:06,834
You'll remember me.

647
01:44:07,045 --> 01:44:09,645
You won't be able to kill me.

648
01:44:11,713 --> 01:44:14,713
I'll live in your hearts.

649
01:44:27,131 --> 01:44:30,181
Burn in hell, ignoble man.

650
01:44:36,103 --> 01:44:39,513
I will take revenge of my son.

651
01:44:42,845 --> 01:44:45,615
I appreciate you Lena.

652
01:44:46,855 --> 01:44:50,125
You let go of my pain.

653
01:44:56,801 --> 01:44:59,761
This is for my son Bayhoca.

654
01:45:27,430 --> 01:45:29,310
Vengeance...

655
01:45:32,445 --> 01:45:35,185
and a sweet dream.

656
01:45:37,587 --> 01:45:41,357
A dream that I don't want to wake up.

657
01:45:45,419 --> 01:45:50,989
A flavour I won't forget...

658
01:45:51,776 --> 01:45:54,556
the taste of.

659
01:45:59,287 --> 01:46:01,257
Die!

660
01:46:03,247 --> 01:46:04,607
Die!

661
01:46:19,078 --> 01:46:21,508
My Bey, what have you done?

662
01:46:21,514 --> 01:46:25,142
Farewell, Lena.

663
01:46:25,142 --> 01:46:27,442
Farewell.

664
01:46:41,370 --> 01:46:44,070
My Bey!

665
01:47:25,774 --> 01:47:27,574
Can I come, my Bey?

666
01:47:28,260 --> 01:47:29,320
Come in.

667
01:47:49,298 --> 01:47:51,148
Tell me, Boran Alp.

668
01:47:52,021 --> 01:47:54,001
What happened?

669
01:47:55,344 --> 01:47:57,144
Flatyos.

670
01:47:57,570 --> 01:47:59,490
What happened to him?

671
01:48:30,498 --> 01:48:33,068
Do you want to see my anger?

672
01:48:34,535 --> 01:48:36,095
What happened to him?

673
01:48:37,156 --> 01:48:38,726
I killed him.

674
01:48:43,211 --> 01:48:45,271
- We killed him.
- Lena!

675
01:48:47,997 --> 01:48:50,687
We took our son's revenge.

676
01:48:57,998 --> 01:48:59,308
What did you do?

677
01:49:07,970 --> 01:49:10,040
What did you do, brother?

678
01:49:24,050 --> 01:49:25,620
Brother.

679
01:49:29,885 --> 01:49:32,325
Why didn't you listen to me?

680
01:49:34,753 --> 01:49:36,343
Why?

681
01:49:36,778 --> 01:49:39,438
Every breath he took was a torture to me.

682
01:49:39,691 --> 01:49:41,771
I couldn't resist.

683
01:49:43,147 --> 01:49:45,377
Do whatever you want.

684
01:50:07,119 --> 01:50:09,669
It's not just about Flatyos.

685
01:50:12,587 --> 01:50:15,197
It's not just about Flatyos.

686
01:50:16,366 --> 01:50:19,416
A traitor from my tent...

687
01:50:19,748 --> 01:50:25,428
is involved in the murder of my nephew.

688
01:50:26,153 --> 01:50:27,923
Brother...

689
01:50:29,565 --> 01:50:31,465
Tell me.

690
01:50:33,246 --> 01:50:37,246
What happens now? Brother?

691
01:50:37,890 --> 01:50:40,090
How will we find that traitor?

692
01:50:40,210 --> 01:50:44,860
Every breath he takes will be
torture to us.

693
01:50:46,498 --> 01:50:48,418
Tell me.

694
01:51:08,589 --> 01:51:10,089
Bala!

695
01:51:12,141 --> 01:51:13,701
Lena!

696
01:51:14,113 --> 01:51:15,803
Lena!

697
01:51:17,411 --> 01:51:19,491
The baby is coming!

698
01:51:20,497 --> 01:51:25,897
Boran Alp. Tell Hatuns to bring warm
water and clean cloth. Come on!

699
01:52:01,940 --> 01:52:07,620
O Gazriin Ezen... (According to Tengrism, the earth is the home of a great variety of spirits, including Gazriin Ezen.)

700
01:52:12,206 --> 01:52:16,206
When the black hawk sings...

701
01:52:21,406 --> 01:52:25,406
When the black hawk sings...

702
01:52:42,912 --> 01:52:48,712
When the black shaman brings death...

703
01:53:11,670 --> 01:53:14,390
Black Shaman Togay.

704
01:54:12,260 --> 01:54:15,980
There was more time.

705
01:54:17,409 --> 01:54:20,199
She's early, Osman Bey.

706
01:54:23,301 --> 01:54:25,801
What if something happens to Lena?

707
01:54:26,681 --> 01:54:28,861
What if something happens to my child?

708
01:54:32,848 --> 01:54:35,168
Don't worry.

709
01:54:35,181 --> 01:54:36,641
Don't worry.

710
01:54:36,694 --> 01:54:41,074
He's hurrying up to help his father.

711
01:54:43,455 --> 01:54:45,175
Yes.

712
01:54:45,691 --> 01:54:49,971
He's coming to relieve your wounds.

713
01:54:50,463 --> 01:54:53,023
- Inshallah, brother.
- Inshallah.

714
01:55:11,208 --> 01:55:14,668
Thank Allah.

715
01:55:16,230 --> 01:55:19,990
Thank Allah...

716
01:55:57,742 --> 01:55:59,722
Mashallah!

717
01:56:00,050 --> 01:56:02,880
His uncle dies for him.

718
01:56:04,804 --> 01:56:07,784
Bala Hatun...

719
01:56:09,796 --> 01:56:12,806
Don't worry.

720
01:56:13,629 --> 01:56:15,549
It's a boy.

721
01:56:17,162 --> 01:56:20,962
- Mashallah.
- Mashallah.

722
01:56:28,817 --> 01:56:32,167
Is Lena Hatun okay?
- Thank Allah, she is.

723
01:57:07,363 --> 01:57:09,373
My son.

724
01:57:12,524 --> 01:57:14,534
My son.

725
01:57:16,450 --> 01:57:18,320
My son.

726
01:57:28,120 --> 01:57:30,410
My son.

727
01:57:36,176 --> 01:57:39,646
Look, brother.
I have a son.

728
01:57:42,317 --> 01:57:45,097
You have a nephew.

729
01:58:04,339 --> 01:58:06,529
Congratulations, brother.

730
01:58:08,097 --> 01:58:10,877
Congratulations.

731
01:58:19,183 --> 01:58:23,183
Savcı brother. I should
take him to his mother.

732
01:58:28,888 --> 01:58:31,358
I will come with you.

733
01:58:55,511 --> 01:58:58,471
My Osman Bey...

734
01:58:58,872 --> 01:59:02,872
Allah's miracles are countless.

735
01:59:02,994 --> 01:59:08,224
Allah gives and takes everything.

736
02:00:11,754 --> 02:00:16,414
Kongar, you'll go to forest spirits
that bring death.

737
02:00:25,148 --> 02:00:29,148
Geyhatu never forgives betrayal!

738
02:00:29,755 --> 02:00:33,085
I'll send you to the
hell you have come from, Togay!

739
02:01:00,804 --> 02:01:04,664
For the black storm!

740
02:01:17,048 --> 02:01:27,538
"In the name of Allah, the Most
Gracious, the Most Merciful."

741
02:01:30,439 --> 02:01:39,959
"Never say that those martyred in
the cause of Allah are dead...

742
02:01:41,382 --> 02:01:44,092
...in fact, they are alive...

743
02:01:44,602 --> 02:01:47,782
with their Lord, well provided for
rejoicing in Allah’s bounties

744
02:01:47,782 --> 02:01:51,142
and being delighted for those
yet to join them.

745
02:01:51,206 --> 02:02:03,196
There will be no fear for
them ...

746
02:02:03,358 --> 02:02:17,238
nor will they grieve...

747
02:02:17,344 --> 02:02:26,254
They are joyful.

748
02:02:28,835 --> 02:02:32,835
Allah said, how good and true way.

749
02:02:34,056 --> 02:02:39,176
"Glorified is your Lord—the Lord of Honour and Power—above what they claim!"

750
02:02:39,564 --> 02:02:43,564
Peace be upon...

751
02:02:44,622 --> 02:02:49,592
the messengers...

752
02:02:50,134 --> 02:02:57,264
And praise be to
Allah—Lord of all worlds."

753
02:02:58,072 --> 02:03:00,542
Al-Fatihah.

754
02:03:36,604 --> 02:03:41,144
Dying is to live out.

755
02:03:41,828 --> 02:03:46,368
It is to give your life to its owner.

756
02:03:47,790 --> 02:03:51,790
Martyrs are witnesses.

757
02:03:52,828 --> 02:03:58,028
They pray with their blood
and wait for Allah's news.

758
02:03:59,393 --> 02:04:02,533
Don't call them "the dead."

759
02:04:02,638 --> 02:04:05,478
Because they're alive.

760
02:04:05,885 --> 02:04:09,565
You don't see it.

761
02:04:10,333 --> 02:04:14,943
They are with Allah.

762
02:04:18,722 --> 02:04:22,452
Allah said that.

763
02:04:22,748 --> 02:04:25,308
You don't see.

764
02:04:25,443 --> 02:04:29,843
Bayhoca is alive and he is happy.

765
02:04:42,425 --> 02:04:45,285
He was...

766
02:04:46,235 --> 02:04:48,025
brave...

767
02:04:49,747 --> 02:04:51,777
like his ancestors.

768
02:04:53,072 --> 02:04:55,992
He was manful.

769
02:04:56,594 --> 02:04:59,494
He always wanted to fight.

770
02:05:03,789 --> 02:05:06,539
He chose martyrdom.

771
02:05:08,880 --> 02:05:11,880
He left Kayı tent...

772
02:05:14,927 --> 02:05:18,927
for the Prophet.

773
02:05:24,386 --> 02:05:26,466
May Allah...

774
02:05:26,891 --> 02:05:29,941
forgive his sins.

775
02:05:29,989 --> 02:05:31,809
Amin.

776
02:05:31,970 --> 02:05:37,950
May Allah grant us martyrdom.

777
02:05:39,117 --> 02:05:43,117
Amin.

778
02:05:55,894 --> 02:05:58,264
Bayhoca.

779
02:06:31,405 --> 02:06:33,825
Bayhoca.

780
02:06:44,449 --> 02:06:46,959
Look, son.

781
02:06:47,274 --> 02:06:51,274
Your brother is a hero.

782
02:06:53,106 --> 02:06:56,116
He couldn't see you.

783
02:07:03,710 --> 02:07:06,180
He couldn't.

784
02:07:13,156 --> 02:07:16,856
For those who believe, there is
no separation.

785
02:07:17,203 --> 02:07:19,383
He'll see him.

786
02:07:23,633 --> 02:07:26,353
A bird comes...

787
02:07:30,184 --> 02:07:32,154
another bird flies.

788
02:07:33,610 --> 02:07:36,800
I was in a place full of white.

789
02:07:36,925 --> 02:07:39,205
Pure white.

790
02:07:39,349 --> 02:07:43,659
A bird came out of my mouth.
It flew.

791
02:07:44,758 --> 02:07:50,198
It became invisible.

792
02:07:51,345 --> 02:07:54,705
It's like it was flying from
a cage, mother.

793
02:07:58,467 --> 02:08:00,857
It flew.

794
02:08:05,041 --> 02:08:08,721
He'll know what a valiant his brother was.

795
02:08:11,176 --> 02:08:14,436
He'll try to be valiant like him.

796
02:08:16,410 --> 02:08:18,440
Inshallah.

797
02:08:18,738 --> 02:08:20,628
Inshallah.

798
02:08:22,796 --> 02:08:31,736
- Peace and prayer be upon
you, o Messenger of Allah. -

799
02:08:32,805 --> 02:08:36,155
We should bury him.

800
02:08:38,965 --> 02:08:41,475
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim. (In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful.)

801
02:08:42,080 --> 02:08:44,220
Come on, Lena.

802
02:08:45,340 --> 02:08:49,340
No!
Don't!

803
02:08:50,340 --> 02:08:53,780
No, no.

804
02:08:53,821 --> 02:08:57,261
Don't take him, please!

805
02:08:57,590 --> 02:09:00,910
Bayhoca. No!

806
02:09:02,346 --> 02:09:09,676
- Peace and prayer be upon
you, o Messenger of Allah. -

807
02:09:10,123 --> 02:09:15,573
No! No!
Please don't take him!

808
02:09:22,243 --> 02:09:28,403
Don't take him! Please!
I beg you!

809
02:09:31,233 --> 02:09:35,993
Don't take him!

810
02:09:40,810 --> 02:09:44,810
Don't take him there!

811
02:11:00,275 --> 02:11:02,305
They are all fake.

812
02:11:26,125 --> 02:11:29,345
Togay doesn't like lies.

813
02:11:30,698 --> 02:11:35,168
Let me go, I'll take you to Osman.

814
02:11:35,907 --> 02:11:39,377
He'll take you to Umur Bey.

815
02:11:40,531 --> 02:11:42,171
How?

816
02:11:42,697 --> 02:11:45,677
I have an informer in the tent.

817
02:11:48,580 --> 02:11:50,490
Dündar.

818
02:11:50,810 --> 02:11:52,900
He is Osman's uncle.

819
02:11:55,079 --> 02:11:57,039
Let's go.

820
02:12:18,610 --> 02:12:21,210
My Bayhoca.

821
02:12:22,053 --> 02:12:25,083
Sleep well, my child.

822
02:12:55,261 --> 02:12:57,441
Sleep well, son.

823
02:12:58,877 --> 02:13:00,557
Sleep well.

824
02:13:02,797 --> 02:13:04,597
Son.

825
02:13:09,301 --> 02:13:11,751
My son.

826
02:13:35,287 --> 02:13:37,167
My child.

827
02:13:44,864 --> 02:13:48,034
You left me...

828
02:13:53,412 --> 02:13:55,652
like the sword flowers...

829
02:13:56,245 --> 02:13:58,785
that blossoms when the sun comes.

830
02:14:00,758 --> 02:14:03,458
You left me.

831
02:14:05,324 --> 02:14:08,674
I couldn't get enough of you, son.

832
02:14:12,766 --> 02:14:15,026
I couldn't.

833
02:14:21,169 --> 02:14:23,379
I couldn't.

834
02:14:38,525 --> 02:14:41,145
Your soil...

835
02:15:07,611 --> 02:15:09,831
I will water your soil..

836
02:15:12,828 --> 02:15:15,598
with my tears, son.

837
02:15:44,804 --> 02:15:47,304
Don't worry, son.

838
02:15:50,357 --> 02:15:52,467
We took your revenge.

839
02:15:54,874 --> 02:15:58,154
We killed...

840
02:15:59,802 --> 02:16:01,642
the murderer of our life.

841
02:16:06,653 --> 02:16:08,713
Me and your mother...

842
02:16:22,939 --> 02:16:25,649
We took your revenge, son.

843
02:16:28,138 --> 02:16:30,728
We took your revenge.

844
02:16:32,893 --> 02:16:35,723
Rest in peace.

845
02:16:39,193 --> 02:16:42,433
Rest in peace, son.

846
02:17:09,508 --> 02:17:13,108
What will we do without you?

847
02:17:15,771 --> 02:17:19,011
What will we do without you?

848
02:17:42,632 --> 02:17:46,802
You made big promises in front of me...

849
02:17:46,821 --> 02:17:51,361
and you convinced us that you
were the right person.

850
02:17:52,433 --> 02:17:55,683
When I heard that you
took over Kulucahisar...

851
02:17:55,698 --> 02:17:59,278
I felt that I gave the
duty to the right person.

852
02:17:59,709 --> 02:18:02,309
You gave Kulucahisar back to Osman.

853
02:18:02,378 --> 02:18:05,928
You caused my soldiers to be killed by
Turks.

854
02:18:06,166 --> 02:18:09,486
Osman is planning to occupy İnegöl.

855
02:18:09,701 --> 02:18:13,351
You promised victory!
Is this victory?

856
02:18:15,019 --> 02:18:18,139
Answer me, Nikola.

857
02:18:24,957 --> 02:18:30,927
When you summoned me, I defeated Osman.

858
02:18:33,228 --> 02:18:35,838
I killed his soldiers...

859
02:18:35,959 --> 02:18:39,089
and I won a victory.

860
02:18:43,481 --> 02:18:46,741
- What?
- I have news for Nikola.

861
02:18:46,831 --> 02:18:48,741
Tell us.

862
02:18:54,103 --> 02:18:56,163
Osman got out of the trap.

863
02:18:56,492 --> 02:19:00,492
Flatyos was taken to Kayı tent.

864
02:19:07,373 --> 02:19:11,673
- Is this the victory you talk about?
- Flatyos...

865
02:19:12,523 --> 02:19:14,553
Another incompetent one.

866
02:19:18,491 --> 02:19:20,851
Incompetent?

867
02:19:22,019 --> 02:19:24,749
I give you one last chance, Nikola.

868
02:19:25,118 --> 02:19:27,338
You will work with someone.

869
02:19:27,338 --> 02:19:30,338
Kalanoz's brother.

870
02:19:30,442 --> 02:19:33,262
A valiant member of Kalanozs.

871
02:19:33,432 --> 02:19:35,752
Efaristos Kalanoz.

872
02:19:35,888 --> 02:19:39,568
Go and empower İnegöl.

873
02:19:40,953 --> 02:19:45,893
If you let Osman take İnegöl, you'll die.

874
02:19:46,120 --> 02:19:48,070
Don't forget that.

875
02:19:48,729 --> 02:19:52,069
Act like a soldier, Nikola!

876
02:19:52,122 --> 02:19:56,122
I won't act like a soldier, Emperor.

877
02:19:56,348 --> 02:19:58,748
I will act like a lion...

878
02:19:59,488 --> 02:20:04,488
I'll kill Osman and his loved ones!

879
02:20:16,439 --> 02:20:19,489
We still don't know who the traitor is.

880
02:20:23,833 --> 02:20:26,343
I'll kill him.

881
02:20:27,823 --> 02:20:29,803
It's not the end.

882
02:20:31,224 --> 02:20:35,224
You're right, Osman Bey.
You're right.

883
02:20:35,712 --> 02:20:39,712
Who'd think that the potter is a traitor?

884
02:20:40,030 --> 02:20:41,890
We'll be careful.

885
02:20:42,057 --> 02:20:46,057
We'll suspect everything and everyone.

886
02:20:46,199 --> 02:20:50,769
We'll follow every trace
and every suspicion.

887
02:20:51,360 --> 02:20:55,700
Until we find that traitor.

888
02:20:59,774 --> 02:21:02,694
I gave Göktuğ a duty.

889
02:21:03,385 --> 02:21:05,545
However, there's still no news.

890
02:21:07,290 --> 02:21:09,940
What kind of duty, Osman Bey?

891
02:21:12,684 --> 02:21:15,044
They want documents.

892
02:21:15,795 --> 02:21:19,055
Göktuğ will deceive Helen with these.

893
02:21:19,132 --> 02:21:23,482
Then they will bring Göktuğ to those
who want the documents.

894
02:21:26,471 --> 02:21:29,941
It's a difficult duty.
Difficult.

895
02:21:30,332 --> 02:21:33,492
I hope they won't harm Göktuğ.

896
02:21:33,788 --> 02:21:36,168
You're right.

897
02:21:38,228 --> 02:21:39,968
You're right.

898
02:21:44,611 --> 02:21:47,911
There's something wrong.

899
02:21:51,167 --> 02:21:52,967
Brother...

900
02:21:53,177 --> 02:21:55,807
Go with the Alps.

901
02:21:56,195 --> 02:21:58,555
Find Göktuğ for me.

902
02:22:00,921 --> 02:22:04,921
Don't worry, Osman Bey.
Your command.

903
02:22:05,051 --> 02:22:05,801
Thank you.

904
02:22:06,104 --> 02:22:08,424
Can I come in, Osman Bey?

905
02:22:10,075 --> 02:22:12,365
Come in.

906
02:22:19,001 --> 02:22:20,831
Tell me, Malhun Hatun.

907
02:23:00,851 --> 02:23:04,131
My father is about to arrive.

908
02:23:04,212 --> 02:23:08,952
He's coming here for your promises.
I want to visit him if you let me.

909
02:23:25,013 --> 02:23:29,013
Good.
I want to see Umur Bey.

910
02:23:29,775 --> 02:23:32,185
We should go together.

911
02:23:33,858 --> 02:23:36,918
My father will come to see you, Osman Bey.

912
02:23:37,163 --> 02:23:39,333
Don't bother.

913
02:23:52,478 --> 02:23:55,248
What do you mean, Malhun Hatun?

914
02:23:56,170 --> 02:24:00,170
I mean that only three of us know that my
father is coming here.

915
02:24:05,177 --> 02:24:10,587
Malhun Hatun believes that the traitor is
someone close to you, Osman Bey.

916
02:24:19,196 --> 02:24:20,976
You...

917
02:24:22,844 --> 02:24:26,971
- want to protect your father.
- His Alps are with him.

918
02:24:27,121 --> 02:24:30,401
However, they are few in number.
They are coming.

919
02:24:30,904 --> 02:24:33,814
I don't want to endanger my father.

920
02:24:35,307 --> 02:24:38,327
No one should know where we are going.

921
02:24:39,097 --> 02:24:41,217
Don't worry.

922
02:24:41,895 --> 02:24:44,275
No one will know.

923
02:24:45,526 --> 02:24:51,586
Your father and your people will come
here safe and sound.

924
02:24:52,210 --> 02:24:54,420
My Alps will ensure safety.

925
02:24:54,641 --> 02:24:57,591
Then I should be prepared.

926
02:25:16,326 --> 02:25:20,746
The Great Osman Bey will
welcome Umur Bey, huh?

927
02:25:27,821 --> 02:25:30,911
I won't welcome a Bey...

928
02:25:31,694 --> 02:25:36,214
I will see the important part of
the army that I will build.

929
02:25:37,258 --> 02:25:40,228
Take care then, Osman Bey.

930
02:25:41,806 --> 02:25:45,166
I hope you return quickly.

931
02:25:52,422 --> 02:25:54,222
Bala Hatun.

932
02:26:02,388 --> 02:26:05,908
Ever since Malhun Hatun came here...

933
02:26:06,704 --> 02:26:09,154
you've been cold towards me.

934
02:26:14,025 --> 02:26:15,045
My Bey.

935
02:26:15,129 --> 02:26:18,249
She looks at everywhere.

936
02:26:18,508 --> 02:26:21,868
She's everywhere, wherever I go.

937
02:26:22,785 --> 02:26:24,275
Bala.

938
02:26:25,002 --> 02:26:28,382
Ever since she came, she has witnessed
many betrayals.

939
02:26:30,687 --> 02:26:35,147
She's right to worry about her tent.

940
02:26:37,897 --> 02:26:41,437
I don't trust anyone
who doesn't trust you.

941
02:26:51,008 --> 02:26:53,768
Have a nice journey.

942
02:27:13,859 --> 02:27:15,579
Can I come in?

943
02:27:16,458 --> 02:27:19,008
Come in.

944
02:27:31,687 --> 02:27:36,297
How could a big army let Osman go?

945
02:27:36,979 --> 02:27:42,079
He was defeated.

946
02:27:43,427 --> 02:27:46,717
Everyone saw his defeat.

947
02:27:47,609 --> 02:27:51,609
- It's a victory for you, Dündar Bey.
- What victory?

948
02:27:52,025 --> 02:27:54,565
He caught Flatyos.

949
02:27:58,201 --> 02:28:03,541
I'm sure he didn't talk.

950
02:28:04,016 --> 02:28:06,366
Savcı handled it.

951
02:28:06,565 --> 02:28:10,925
Our Alps are dead. They were my children.

952
02:28:15,205 --> 02:28:18,355
I feel sorry.

953
02:28:20,010 --> 02:28:24,010
You don't have much time to...

954
02:28:25,161 --> 02:28:27,651
clean the blood on
your hands with Osman's blood.

955
02:28:27,769 --> 02:28:31,699
- Osman will find out sooner or later.
- Don't worry.

956
02:28:33,169 --> 02:28:40,279
Osman has a big enemy now.

957
02:28:43,375 --> 02:28:45,125
Who?

958
02:28:49,180 --> 02:28:51,880
Geyhatu's hunter dog...

959
02:28:52,334 --> 02:28:55,574
the Black Shaman Togay.

960
02:30:24,816 --> 02:30:30,386
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com